4.4.4   Solving the Model
In this model, parameters which need to solve are: k, nup , ndown , µ, Σ. The magnitude of
wup , wdown can be accessed by physical analysis.




                                                                                                                                                                  2
                                                                                                                                                                      关注数学模型
                                                                                                                                                         MATHmodels


                                                                                                                                                                      获取更多资讯
Team # 2501567                                                                Page 15 of 24


If the change in log-likelihood between iterations is smaller than a predefined threshold
(e.g., ϵ), then we reach the maximized value of and get the proper value of πi , µi , Σi .
   Once the value of πi is accessible,
                         ZZ                                     ZZ
                    πi k                                   πi k
         nup + εi =          W (x, y) dx dy, ndown + εi =          W (x, y) dx dy           (27)
                    wup                                   wdown
                           D                                     D

Error term εi can be eliminated by regression respectively. Then the certain direction of
travel favored by the people using the stairs is:

   • upstairs, if nup > ndown , or

   • downstairs, if nup < ndown .

   However, the solution process above is based on the certain value of k. To specify the
value of k, we will use Bayesian Information Criterion (BIC):

                                     BIC = p ln M − 2l                                      (28)

where p is the total number of parameters, M is the total number of the data point, and
is the maximized value of the log-likelihood function.
    Initially, we set the proper range I for k, e.g. 1 ≤ k ≤ 10, and for each possible value
of k, compute BIC. Then,
                                       k = arg min BIC                                  (29)
                                              k∈I




