4.9     Frequency and Duration Patterns




                                                             型
4.9.1   Chaboche Model
In structural engineering, fatigue damage is a critical consideration, especially when




                                                           模
components are subjected to repetitive loading. For staircases, two common types of
loading scenarios are short-duration high-frequency stepping and long-duration low-




                                                         学
frequency stepping, each of which affects the structure in distinct ways [11]. The former
causes rapid, high-magnitude impacts that may lead to sudden localized damage, while




                                                       数
the latter involves prolonged, lower-magnitude stresses that accumulate over time. Un-
derstanding how these two types of stepping contribute to fatigue damage is essential for




                                                   ：
assessing the long-term durability of staircases. This section aims to explore the fatigue




                                                  el s
damage mechanisms under these different loading conditions.
                                                 号
   The Chaboche model describes the nonlinear hardening behavior of materials using




                                                od
multiple backstress components. The yield function and backstress evolution equations
                                  众
are central to the model:


